Task: Implement generate_plan_cached() function in plan_generator.py (Track 37 Phase 1)

Summary:
Added CacheStatus dataclass (hit: bool, reason: str) and generate_plan_cached()
function to plan_generator.py. The function checks a cached plan.json: if all
discovered .gd files have matching source hashes, the cached plan is reused
without AST parsing (cache hit). Falls back to full generate_plan() on any
file added/deleted/modified, corrupt/missing cache, or use_cache=False.

Files modified:
- src/gd_tools/coverage/plan_generator.py: Added CacheStatus dataclass and
  generate_plan_cached() function (~130 lines)
- tests/unit/test_plan_generator.py: Added 9 cache tests (hit, miss-modified,
  miss-added, miss-deleted, miss-no-file, miss-corrupt, use_cache=False,
  no-cache-path, dataclass fields)

Why: Coverage plan regeneration on every test --coverage run adds latency for
large projects. Hash-based caching skips AST parsing when no source files
changed. Part of Track 37 (Plan Generator Caching), Phase 1.
